# SphereIQ Web App — Agent Rules

## Project Context
- Converting legacy C# WinForms desktop app (SphereIQ / Ezy-Nav) into a cross-platform web application.
- Source C# project remains in the same root (`Ezy-Nav.csproj`, `EzyPlan_Interface_V2/`). Do **not** modify or delete C# source unless intentionally porting logic.
- Target deployment: **Vercel**. Target database: **Neon (PostgreSQL)**.

## Tech Stack (Fixed — do not deviate)
- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router), TypeScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Database: Neon Postgres (serverless)
- ORM: Prisma
- Auth: NextAuth.js (credentials + session)
- Charts: Chart.js / react-chartjs-2
- File storage: Vercel Blob or S3 (for hole file uploads)
- Language: TypeScript only (no C# in the web app)

## Hard Rules
1. No `System.Windows.Forms`, no WinForms, no GDI+, no .NET DLLs in web code.
2. No direct local file system access. All file uploads go through API routes to object storage.
3. All C# business logic must be ported by hand to TypeScript; no compiling C# on the server.
4. Responsive, mobile-friendly UI.
5. API-first design: separate frontend UI from backend API routes within Next.js.
6. Secrets only in `.env.local` / `.env.example`; never commit real values.
7. Conventional commit messages (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, etc.).
8. Each coding step maps to a phase in `plan_web_app.md`.

## Source Code Reference (C# legacy)
- Port from: `Procedure_*.cs`, `Body_*.cs`, `Utility.cs`, `Report_*` (calculation logic only), `EzyPlanData` models.
- Do **not** reference `..\rstudio\2iC Australia\Ezy-Nav\` DLLs.

## Phases (from plan_web_app.md)
1. Project setup & database schema ← CURRENT
2. Authentication & user management
3. Hole file upload & data models
4. Drilling math & survey calculations
5. UI wizard screens (Welcome, Create Hole, Planning, etc.)
6. Reports & charts
7. Testing & Vercel deployment
